 positions to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attached to a graph (LEMON’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ArcMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned by ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph.addEdgeMap(default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It holds no values: read and write them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the graph, ","type":"text"},{"code":"graph[handle, ofEdgeAt: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It is valid on the graph that added it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and on every copy of that graph, until ","type":"text"},{"code":"removeEdgeMap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; on another graph it traps.","type":"text"}],"title":"EdgeMap","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/edgemap","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeMap"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/GraphDelegator":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GraphDelegator"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GraphDelegator"}],"title":"GraphDelegator","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graphdelegator","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphDelegator","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A wrapper that owns its base, keeps the base’s vertices, edges and positions, and adds only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rules: JGraphT’s "},{"code":"GraphDelegator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every read requirement of "},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has a default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that forwards to the base, ","type":"text"},{"code":"@inlinable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and with the base’s own types, so algorithms run at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"base’s speed and data kept by position stays valid through the wrapper. The wrapper implements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation itself (that is where its rules are), and its non-requirement members.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/EdgeValues":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeValues"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeValues"}],"title":"EdgeValues","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/edgevalues","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeValues","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A snapshot of an edge map’s values, read by edge position like an array: what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph.values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns, after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary.Values"},{"type":"text","text":". It holds the map’s storage, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the graph, so later mutations of the graph or the map do not show through."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"}}}